<!-- @opening -->
<p class="story-lead">The first import looks correct. A retry duplicates a workout, and a deleted record comes back from your app’s cache. Health synchronization needs a repeatable local transaction: which records changed, which disappeared, and how far has the import safely committed?</p>

<!-- @after Incremental Synchronization :: animation -->
### Commit data before advancing progress

<figure class="stepper"><span class="stepper-title">One incremental page, with a crash in the middle</span><div class="stage viz-stack"><div class="node" data-el="token"><strong>Saved progress</strong><small data-text="tokenV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="page"><strong>Changes page</strong><small data-text="pageV">—</small></div><div class="node" data-el="db"><strong>App-owned store</strong><small data-text="dbV">—</small></div></div><script type="application/json" class="steps">[
{
"label": "Fetch",
"caption": "Read the next changes page using saved progress T1.",
"state": {
"page": "active"
},
"text": {
"tokenV": "T1",
"pageV": "upsert A; delete B; next T2",
"dbV": "previous state"
},
"add": [
"token",
"page",
"db"
]
},
{
"label": "Apply",
"caption": "Apply upserts and deletions to local storage.",
"state": {
"db": "active"
},
"text": {
"dbV": "A updated; B removed"
}
},
{
"label": "Crash before commit",
"caption": "If the local transaction fails before committing data and progress, replay from the last committed token while it remains valid; otherwise take the reconciliation path.",
"state": {
"db": "warn",
"token": "done"
},
"text": {
"dbV": "transaction rolled back",
"tokenV": "still T1"
}
},
{
"label": "Replay and commit",
"caption": "An idempotent transaction can apply the page again and commit its matching progress.",
"state": {
"db": "done",
"token": "active"
},
"text": {
"dbV": "A updated; B removed",
"tokenV": "T2 after success"
}
},
{
"label": "Token no longer usable",
"caption": "Use the chapter’s bounded reconciliation path when progress expires or is invalid.",
"state": {
"token": "warn"
},
"text": {
"tokenV": "reconcile; do not invent missing history"
}
}
]</script><figcaption>The transaction pattern is application design. Feature availability, permission scope and historical coverage still bound what can be read.</figcaption></figure>

<!-- @after Testing Strategy :: check -->
### Try the decision

<details><summary>No steps returned. User inactive?</summary>

Not necessarily: missing access, data, availability or synchronization can also explain it.
</details>

<details><summary>Token saved before local writes?</summary>

A crash could skip changes. Save matching progress only with successful local application.
</details>

<details><summary>A worker always reads Health Connect?</summary>

Only with the required background-read feature and separate grant; otherwise ingest in the foreground.
</details>
